 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-15", "priority": "P1", "title": "[dogfood:P1] Placeholder probe-regexes are UNANCHORED — any real class whose title CONTAINS 'dogfood'/'canary'/'field-test'/etc. is solved, stored, browsable, but 404s on discover and is INVISIBLE in the queue list", "status": "complete", "detail": "Real-use run 2026-09-23 (scratch :18766, HEAD 239cbdb, seed 2094/2184): submitted two genuine problems ('ob1-dogfood-fib-off-by-one-index', 'ob1-ctx-canary-deploy-oom'). Both solved by the REAL solver (24s / 58s, correct solutions stored, answer ids 2185/2186). Discover (POST /api/v1/problems/discover) returns 404 'problem class not found' for BOTH (fresh-discover 12ms, broad discover also 404) while GET /api/v1/problems/{class}, GET .../answers, and q= search all RETURN them — one defect, three inconsistent symptoms. Root cause: internal/graph/placeholder.go:34 list — regexp.MustCompile('(?i)dogfood') et al. match ANY SUBSTRING of a title, and the same family is applied in SQL via graph.NotPlaceholderClassSQL in ingest/queue.go listQueuePageQuery/listQueueCountQuery/pendingOrderQuery, so the queue list returns entries:null,total:0 while GET /api/v1/queue/{id} returns the entry. IsPlaceholderClass is only meant to quarantine probe classes (self-test/canary/dogfood PROBE families), but with no anchors and no word-boundaries it quarantines every real user whose slug mentions those words. A real user hits this with zero warning: submit 200, solve complete, browse visible, discover 404. Control verified: 'python-pip-interpreter-mismatch-pep668' discovers found:true 10ms. Fix direction: anchor the patterns (self-test/dogfood/canary probes are PREFIX families like off-by-one-self-test-*, test-self-dogfood-*, docs-canary-*, dogfood-field-test-* — anchor to the actual probe prefixes or require exact tokens), keep NotPlaceholderClassSQL in sync, and add a round-trip test: submit->solve->discover must return found:true for a class title merely containing 'dogfood'.", "accepta