 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-16", "priority": "P3", "title": "[dogfood:P3] Web-UI chat returns the answer as a single frame after ~74s with NO interim progress frames — user stares at a frozen chat for over a minute", "status": "pending", "detail": "First exercise of the /ws/chat surface (real WebSocket client, 2026-09-23 scratch :18766): upgrade 101, system hello immediate, then a single agent frame with the full 2932-byte solution at t=74s. Nothing in between except 15s-interval WS pings (which the browser answers invisibly). chat.go deliberately runs the full sandbox+pi-agent cycle synchronously; the 74s silence is the design, but a human user cannot distinguish 'thinking' from 'dead' — and a naive non-browser WS client that skips pongs is disconnected at the first ping (observed). Fix direction: send a 'thinking'/status frame immediately on message receipt and periodic stage updates (searching graph / preparing sandbox / solving), reusing the chat message protocol the UI already renders; document the ping cadence for non-browser clients.", "acceptance_criteria": "A chat message receives at least one interim frame within ~2s of send; the docs mention the server ping cadence; a pong-skipping client is either tolerated or the disconnect is documented.", "created_at": "2026-09-23", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-23-10-59-22 (web-UI chat surface, first exercised this run)", "evidence": "chat_probe3.py transcript: hello immediate, pings t=15/30/45/60s, agent frame t=74.0s bytes=2932; internal/web/chat.go"}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-17", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "title": "[dogfood:P2] Muster consumer path is a dead end for a fresh user — the 'muster' binary is unbuildable from docs and connect-muster.sh reports success without it", "detail": "Run #10 (2026-09-24) exercised the README core-loop step 1 ('Agents push problems via Muster API/MCP/CLI') for the first time. The wire protocol is real: pkg/api/openapi.json drives an independent OpenAPI->MCP client (MusterFlow) into 15 working tools; initialize/tools/list/tools/call discoverSolution all return live data; CLI and MCP submissions land in the same queue as REST. But the bridge's own consumer cannot be installed: scripts/connect-muster.sh says 'go install github.com/wojons/muster@latest' — github.com/wojons/muster is a PRIVATE module with no published tag, so the install fails for every fresh user; the script then prints 'Muster binary not found', skips step 4, and STILL exits 0 with '=== Integration Complete ===' (reproduced on a fresh bunker clone 17a481c, dry-run). Fix direction: publish a muster release binary (same recipe as the off-by-one release lane) OR name the supported consumer (e.g. MusterFlow, which is proven to work) in the README's Muster section and drop the dead go-install line; make the script exit non-zero (or loudly degrade) when muster is absent.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25 (Muster consumer side, first exercised)", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "A fresh user can reach the lab's tools through an MCP client following only repo docs; no doc path instructs `go install` of a private module; connect-muster.sh exits non-zero or prints a named remedy when muster is missing.", "evidence": "docs/dogfood/2026-09-24-integration.md; bunker agent f0557da1 dry-run transcript; musterflow connect 15 endpoints/15 tools; MCP tools/call discoverSolution 200 with full solution"}
-{"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-18", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "title": "[dogfood:P2] connect-muster.sh hardcodes :8766 (would start a second daemon on a collision host) and health-checks :8767, a port pinned by nothing", "detail": "connect-muster.sh step 1 nohups `off-by-one --db <repo>/off-by-one.db` when :8766 is not healthy — on a host where a foreign daemon owns 8766 (the README's own documented collision scenario) a real run would bind-fail at best and, with a different -db default, risk a second writer against shared state. Step 4 then health-checks http://localhost:8767/health, a port nothing in muster-config.yaml (transport: stdio) or any config pins. OFF_BY_ONE_URL overrides the target but is undocumented anywhere in README/docs. Fix direction: derive ports from one config source, honor OFF_BY_ONE_PORT/OFF_BY_ONE_URL consistently, document the env override, and refuse to start a daemon whose health check returns a FOREIGN identity (e.g. check /health then -version) instead of blindly nohuping.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "connect-muster.sh --dry-run --check-only on a port-collision host reports the collision and starts nothing; the health-check port comes from config; OFF_BY_ONE_URL/OFF_BY_ONE_PORT overrides documented in README Configuration.", "evidence": "scripts/connect-muster.sh lines ~46-110; dry-run transcript 2026-09-24 (both ports observed); muster-config.yaml transport stdio"}
